 :question/math-academy-id "q-64747" :question/problem "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as:\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =({e}^{x}){(x{e}^{x})}^{′}-(x{e}^{x}){({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})({e}^{x}+x{e}^{x})-(x{e}^{x})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({e}^{x}+x{e}^{x}-x{e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64747/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ca68460-f3fe-5ae8-b5f4-85742c0ef46b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64747"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334114/field-1/4a5e918ea312eced90c9c1cddfd857ab09d00da4fbc89b8bc177ba3dc139a14b" :answer/id #uuid "1f04b67e-0d70-58d4-ba0f-2bd381d9e75a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334114/field-1/080366e879b141180c5f237b6981b1e7fd8f6d1dc4984535958806c6c6c2944d" :answer/id #uuid "79c8d9af-82c6-5ecf-b9f7-0bdfbc22d681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334114/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c9cee825-29d8-5ad3-97ff-776f8a679d8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334114/field-1/19370c9253530adcb101aa7c26707d5ff9a04952be68f2880b0cc7cfca4a41a0" :answer/id #uuid "090180d9-9124-56a0-9cf5-99a7cf970b26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/